     1	# AGENTS.md — Cross-LLM Reviewer Contract
     2	
     3	Contract for the second-model reviewer on the pair-rail (ADR-107): the
     4	non-Claude LLM (currently Codex) that reviews canonical edits proposed in
     5	this repo, so no single model is both author and sole reviewer. Read this
     6	file before reviewing any diff. Humans: start at [README.md](README.md);
     7	Claude Code sessions: start at [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md).
     8	
     9	This repo is the framework itself, not an installed copy. It makes **no
    10	speed claim** — the value is governance and auditability. Reject any doc
    11	change that adds throughput or speedup claims.
    12	
    13	## 1. Review doctrine
    14	
    15	Check every diff against these rules. Each is enforced by CI or hooks; a
    16	REJECT should cite the rule and the offending `file:line`.
    17	
    18	| Rule | What to check | Defined / enforced |
    19	|---|---|---|
    20	| Stdlib-only runtime | No third-party imports in framework Python (`SBOM.md` lists zero runtime deps) | [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md) §4 · `.claude/scripts/check-stdlib-only.py` |
    21	| Python ≥ 3.9 compatible | `from __future__ import annotations` present; no runtime PEP 604 unions (use `typing.Optional` / `typing.Union`); no `match` statements | [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md) §4 |
    22	| Fail-open on infrastructure | Hooks never block the session on a missing file, import failure, or timeout — breadcrumb + `{}` allow. **Deliberate exception (ADR-186):** the canonical-edit matcher's wall deadline fails CLOSED — a timeout there is an incomplete verification, not infrastructure; recovery = the provenance-pinned unlock | [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md) §4 · [ADR-186](.claude/adr/ADR-186-hook-deadline-policy.md) |
    23	| Fail-closed on input (security matchers) | Content a security matcher cannot parse is BLOCKED, not waved through (precedents in `.claude/hooks/check_bash_safety.py`; codified by PLAN-152 debate C4) | [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md) §4 |
    24	| Env isolation in tests | Tests touching env use `TestEnvContext` (`.claude/hooks/_lib/testing.py`) + `mock.patch.dict` — never direct `os.environ[...] =` writes, never the real `$HOME` / `$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR` | [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md) §4 |
    25	| No contamination | No personal handles or private project names in framework/template content; neutral placeholders only (`Canhada-Labs`, `your-app`); `.github/CODEOWNERS` is the sole live-handle exception | `.claude/scripts/check-contamination.sh` |
    26	| Counts tolerance = 0 | Hardcoded counts in `CLAUDE.md` (skills/hooks/ADRs/commands) and README badges must exactly match disk — flag any count edit not derived from disk | `.claude/scripts/check-claude-md-claims.py` |
    27	
    28	## 2. Action limits
    29	
    30	- **Read-only.** The reviewer never edits, creates, or deletes files in
    31	  this repo; it emits a verdict, nothing else. (Enforced hook-side by
    32	  `.claude/hooks/check_codex_filewrite.py`.)
    33	- **No network.** Reviews run sandboxed against the local checkout only.
    34	- **Verdict form.** Review verdicts are `APPROVE` or `REJECT`; every
    35	  REJECT must cite at least one `file:line` per finding. (The runtime
    36	  hook-level dispatch vocabulary PASS / BLOCK / ADVISORY and the Cases A–F
    37	  matrix live in
    38	  [docs/PAIR-RAIL-VERDICT-MATRIX.md](docs/PAIR-RAIL-VERDICT-MATRIX.md).)
    39	
    40	## 3. Repo map
    41	
    42	One line per directory. The first backtick cell of each row is
    43	machine-checked against disk (see §5).
    44	
    45	<!-- agents-md:repo-map:begin -->
    46	
    47	| Path | What it is |
    48	|---|---|
    49	| `SPEC/` | Published compliance contract (versioned schemas under `SPEC/v1/`) |
