codex
The manifest/allowlist shape itself is coherent: both templates use canonical verdict-fields paths, basename manifests, and the fixed evidence sets match the guard’s set-equality model; the reused `inputs_hash` also excludes every rc.3 cure path. I found failures in the ceremony control flow rather than in that template math.
codex
P1 — `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/OWNER-RC3-CUT.sh:450` — After verifying the detached signature, the script writes `$VD` without rejecting symlinks and never re-verifies `$VF.asc` against `$VF`. A symlink or concurrent replacement can overwrite/change the signed fields; the mismatched signature is then embedded, committed, and accepted by the later guards. Minimal fix: mirror GA steps 3–4—remove/reject stale artifacts, generate through regular temporary files, atomically rename, and re-run `gpg --verify "$VF.asc" "$VF"` immediately before staging.

P1 — `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/OWNER-GA-CUT.sh:50` — Remote GA-tag detection occurs only when a local `v1.3.0` tag exists. If the remote tag exists but the local ref does not, the script performs the re-pass, commits and pushes both GA commits, signs a local tag, and fails only at the tag push. A rerun then aborts on remote/local divergence, leaving main mutated. Minimal fix: query the remote GA tag unconditionally before any mutation; enter monitoring only after fetching and verifying exact tag-object, commit, signature, and HEAD coherence, otherwise abort.

P1 — `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-ga/run-ga-repass.sh:191` — The runner intentionally lacks `set -e`, but `RAW_SHA` computation and the per-part provenance append are unguarded. If `shasum` fails, it records an empty raw-payload pin and continues; `MANIFEST-ga.sha256`, `validate_ga_evidence`, the delta guard, and step 15 all accept that semantically incomplete provenance. Minimal fix: explicitly guard the hash and every provenance write, then require exactly two nonempty 64-hex raw-payload pins during `validate_ga_evidence`.

VERDICT: NO-GO — The rc.3 ceremony can commit mismatched signed material, and the GA path has both late remote-tag discovery and fail-open provenance generation.
